<!DOCTYPE qhelp PUBLIC
  "-//Semmle//qhelp//EN"
  "qhelp.dtd">
<qhelp>
<overview>
<p>
A <code>${expr}</code> interpolation inside one of <code>mkDerivation</code>'s
shell-context attributes is not passed through <code>lib.escapeShellArg</code>
(or an equivalent sanitizer). The build wrapper evaluates phase strings as
Bash, so any unsanitized interpolation is potentially subject to word-splitting
or shell-metacharacter injection.
</p>
<p>
This query is the conservative counterpart of <code>nix/shell-injection-in-build-phase</code>:
where the latter reports flows from specific untrusted sources, this one
flags <em>every</em> interpolation that lacks a sanitizer, regardless of
where the value comes from.
</p>
</overview>

<recommendation>
<p>
Wrap any interpolated value with <code>lib.escapeShellArg</code> if there's
any plausible path by which it could include shell metacharacters or
whitespace.
</p>
</recommendation>

<example>
<sample language="nix">
{ stdenv, lib, pname }:
stdenv.mkDerivation {
  inherit pname;
  buildPhase = ''
    ./configure --name=${lib.escapeShellArg pname}
  '';
}
</sample>
</example>

<references>
<li>
CWE: <a href="https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/77.html">CWE-77</a>,
<a href="https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/78.html">CWE-78</a>
</li>
</references>
</qhelp>
